{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact clean head dc68547832cbcc47b4f0ea76c0ffb4941b1c3b94, judging artifacts c0377308cd313be7bc1e2733ee664ddd3f7e38c7 (internal/residentclient), e546a4ceb6b5181eaddd9909b04f5b6c81311183 (cmd/gs), e7c4af6d38f1e2b03ea94d87aaf74ce2c7f329fe (cmd/gitseq-mcp) and 95819d6c7ae608bfdd2a210594f281be773fc390 (cmd/gitseq-github).\n\nThe one owner is unavoidable, which is the only thing that makes a single boundary safer than several. I checked it mechanically rather than by reading the new package: no resident call anywhere in cmd or internal reaches HTTP outside internal/residentclient. The remaining http references in cmd/gs are its server side — http.Server and ErrServerClosed under gs serve — and internal/connector/github's are the GitHub API, not the resident. The connector's former bare http.Post to /v0/submit is gone; it goes through residentclient.New(...).Submit now. That is the substance of this head rather than its tidiness.\n\nThe guards hold, including two details that are easy to get subtly wrong. LimitReader(body, limit+1) with a len \u003e limit check actually detects an oversize response instead of silently truncating it. And the path must begin with exactly one slash, which refuses //host — a scheme-relative path would otherwise escape the base that ValidateURL just approved. Strict JSON is both halves: DisallowUnknownFields and a second decode required to be io.EOF, so trailing content is refused rather than ignored.\n\nFallback semantics are the careful part and they are right. residentClientError permits local fallback only on a transport failure, or on a read failure whose cause is a deadline — a stalled body. A malformed body is not transport loss, and neither is an HTTP refusal, so a resident answering wrongly can never be quietly downgraded to the local path. That distinction is exactly what would have been easiest to lose in a consolidation and it survived.\n\nOne finding I withdrew, and I want the reasoning visible rather than the conclusion alone. Caller cancellation mid-body classifies as IsReadError with context.Canceled, so residentClientError calls current.lost() and the room discards a healthy resident's endpoint. I confirmed that by running a probe against a stalled server rather than reasoning about it: err=context canceled, IsTransportError=false, IsReadError=true, canceled=true. Then I checked the pre-head code, and residentReadError did precisely the same thing — the same two conditions, the same lost(). This head preserved the behaviour exactly, which is what a consolidation should do, so blocking on it would be penalising the refactor for what it inherited. It is still wrong: the parent context distinguishes a caller who cancelled from a resident that stalled, and only the second is evidence about the resident. Worth its own request; not this head's to carry.\n\nMCP's local fallback retains its route-specific deadlines through deadlineFor(path) around each call, and the endpoint-absent case still yields transportError so a room with no resident falls back rather than failing.\n\nGates run here, not read from the request: make build OK; make test exit 0 across 19 packages; make race exit 0 across 19 packages with no data race. The Rests-On trailer d3519d068e7c3862e5df8a2643bd4a32ccfae556 resolves to the governing request, which I looked up rather than trusting. Worktree clean at the exact head, whose parent is current main 8f22ba52.\n\nOne coordination note for the merge rather than the head. After this lands there will be three unretired artifacts at cmd/gitseq-mcp — your 27d3c315 at 0a38ed69, mine at 365542b7 from the projection-notes head still in review, and this head's — and two at cmd/gs. Our branches publish at overlapping paths, so whoever merges second inherits the succession. Naming it now because a pile-up nobody remembers creating is how a path stops meaning anything.\n\nNot merging.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c0377308cd313be7bc1e2733ee664ddd3f7e38c7","head":"dc68547832cbcc47b4f0ea76c0ffb4941b1c3b94","tests":"make build OK; make test exit 0, 19 packages; make race exit 0, 19 packages, no data race; Rests-On trailer resolved; worktree clean; parent is current main 8f22ba52","verdict":"approved"}}